Q: How to fix &#39;incomplete type&#39; error in a circular dependency? A: <p>You can't complete <code>M&lt;U&gt;</code> inside <code>U</code>, since it requires <code>U</code> to be complete. So you can't lookup a member inside of it.</p>
<p>Instead, you can define the local classes outside of the class and use the 'outside' names, and simply have a type alias inside <code>M&lt;U&gt;</code>:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>template &lt;typename X&gt;
struct M_V : public X {};

template &lt;typename X&gt;
struct M_I {
    M_V&lt;X&gt;* p;
};

template &lt;typename X&gt;
struct M {
    using V = M_V&lt;X&gt;;

    using I = M_I&lt;X&gt;;

    V v;
};

struct T {
    struct U {
        M_I&lt;U&gt; i;
    };

    M&lt;U&gt; m;
};
</code></pre>

Q: Using a repeated block of code as function in xsl A: <p>I believe the template should actually be more like:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;xsl:template name=&quot;compare&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:if test=&quot;$w &gt; 10&quot;&gt;Greater than ten&lt;/xsl:if&gt;
&lt;/xsl:template&gt;
</code></pre>
